{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Of every clean beast you shall take for yourself, etc.</b> The verse's saying <b>you shall take for yourself</b> intends to say two things: first, that he himself is to exert effort to take the extra seven [pairs]; and the reason given is that they are for his own needs, as the verse says <b>for yourself</b> — for your needs. Through this, it is not difficult [to answer] who permitted Noah to offer a sacrifice from the animals without the Master's permission, for these HaShem commanded for the survival of the species. Or it may be that since the reason for there being seven is that the world needs them more, HaShem would have commanded to keep seven of them and not for a sacrifice. Rather, in what HaShem inscribed and said, ״תִּקַּח לְךָ,״ He showed him that they are for his own needs; therefore he did with them as he desired and offered them to HaShem, and he succeeded in his sacrifice and it was accepted for him. And if he also wishes to eat of them, he may slaughter and eat, for meat was permitted to him for a reason that I will explain with HaShem's help (Genesis 9:3)."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:40:00.238071823Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}